Message-ID: <9601051743.AA15494@frodo.eng.pko.dec.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jan 1996 12:43:26 -0500 (EST)
From: Kevin A. Mocklin <mocklin@frodo.eng.pko.dec.com>
Subject: Re: ALPHA Firmware

> > Last friday I updated the firmware on our two ALPHA 2100 NT servers. I used
> > the 3.3 CD that DEC puts out.  I have some questions and comments.
> > 
> > 1.  When ever you update the firmware there is mention to use a clear*
> > console command after the
> >      update and before running the ECU disk.  Is this a must?  Some of the
> > readme files talk mention
> >      it while others do not.
> 
> This is NOT necessary anymore.  Quite a few revs back of the firmware
> had some inconsistencies between the SRM and ARC consoles after an
> upgrade that the clear* command cleaned up.  This has been incorporated
> into the normal firmware upgrade, so the clear* command is not
> necessary.  I do not remember exactly what version of the firmware
> began upgrading clean, but it was a while ago.  If you need the exact
> version, I can dig it up.

I need to clarify this a bit.  Whether or not you need to use the
clear_arc_nvram command after a firmware upgrade is determined by the
version of ARC firmware that you are upgrading *from*, not to.  If you
are upgrading from ARC version 4.25 or later (bundled with SRM version
4.0, and found on V3.2 firmware CD), then you should not need to issue
the clear* commands.  If you are upgrading from an earlier version,
then the clear* commands should be issued as described in the firmware
release notes.  Remember that this info is relavent for the
AlphaServer 2100.

Sorry about any confusion.

thanks,
Kevin

