Subject: Re: real audio

Presently, the Sound Blaster 16 is the only sound card available for the
Alpha. You are not the only one having problems in this area. Take note that
many sound board manufacturers will port their drivers to the Alpha in the
first quarter of this year. 

First on the list is the Turtle Beach Tahiti. You will be in luck if you
have one of these cards lying around since the driver will probably be
available this month. If you don't have one of these cards, don't try and
get one since they have been discontinued. For more information on this
driver you can contact Hall Sound Systems at 75430.2014@compuserve.com.

I also understand that Digital Audio Labs is working on an Alpha driver for
the Card D. No information on this other than that. 

On the high end side, Antex is also reportedly working on Alpha drivers.
They can be reached at www.antex.com

For those that want to sync audio with video using the Perception Video
Recorder, DPS plans to release their A4V audio card in the spring. For more
info on this contact www.dps-inc.com

