the larger NTFS partition as the C: drive, i.e., create a partition
of DriveSize-6Mbytes as your first partition, then create the system 
(FAT) partition second.  That way, you will not have a C: drive that's 
too small to hold all the third-party software that defaults to it. 
You don't have the choice to omit the system partition, so your best 
option is to simply put it out of the way.

Note that ARCINST does not format the larger partition as an NTFS
partition; it only knows about FAT.  You specify the formatting of
the large partition as NTFS at Windows NT installation time.

Cheers,
James

