>want to use NTFS, I make a second partition for that.
>
>It seems inelegant to leave a tiny C: drive on the system, and I imagine
>there must be a better way to do this. Any ideas out there?

You don't have to do it you can make the entire drive "C".  However, its
best to create a 5-to-10Mb FAT system partition and remainder for NTFS for
the NT files. You can also split the drive again to about 200 for NTFS than
create another drive for applications only.

So on large drives you would have something like this:

        C: 5-to-10 FAT
        D: 200mb NTFS
        E: 200mb-to-remainder of disk

Hope this helps!

