>     I was recently working on a couple of dual processor 2100 machines
>     running NT server 3.51.  I noticed they seemed to be quite sluggish;
>     for example, bringing up SQL enterprise would result in a screen
>     redraw that could take several seconds.  After spending about 2 hours
>     with the performance monitor, I came up with nothing.  Processor
>     seemed fine, disk seemed OK.  Not much going on with these machines.

More than likely this has nothing to do with the actual processor or I/O
speed, but rather the cirrus logic clinear video chip that comes with most
AlphaServers.  Screen redraw speed is mainly a function of the video
subsystem, in general.  Since the machine is intended to be a server and
not a workstation, 512k cirrus logic (600x800x256@72Hz) video is more than
adequate.  If youre spoiled by faster video, you can always opt to install
an S3-based video card, though you would have to make sure you had
appropriate drivers.

