As for switch settings I seemed to get the best results when I set the rear 
SBB switches so the device is configured as device 1.

There are a set of jumpers named J2 that are configured as follows:

Switches DS & ME are NOT jumpered.  This means that the "spindle starts 
immediately after power up - Default setting."

Switch PE (Parity Checking)  is jumpered and therefore on.

Switches TP & TP  there are 2 of them are currently configured with TP left 
jumpered and
TP right NOT jumpered.  This seems very important.

The 2 switches can be configured in the following ways:

     TP   TP   

     Off  Off  No Terminator power is connect to drive terminators or SCSI 
bus I/O
               pin 26

     On   Off  Drive supplies its own terminator power only.
               Jumper on this position is factory DEFAULT for "N" models 
only.

     ON   ON   Drive supplies terminator power to itself (internal 
connection)
               and to I/O pin 26 of SCSI bus.  This is a legal jumper 
setting.

     ON        (this is where a jumper across the two lower pins)
               This horizontally positioned jumper across the two TP
               postions nearest PCB edge, connects terminator power from
               SCSI bus I/O pin 26 to drive's internal terminators.
     Off       See above explanation

