All,

This response is unfortunately a red herring, in that there is
no Alpha server product, other than the AlphaServer 1000, which
has an integral VGA, as described below.  In particular, the 
AlphaServer 2100 family does not have an integral VGA of any 
sort, Cirrus Logic Linear 5422 or otherwise.  It is possible,
of course, that the video adapter installed in this 2100 is one
with weak performance, but it's much more likely that the system
is in a network that's having problems, thus causing the Windows 
NT redirector to consume excessive amounts of CPU time, starving
user-mode processes.

Cheers,
James

