>      NetBEUI IS NOT NEEDED. PERIOD!!!  NetBios is needed!! They are NOT the 
>      same thing!!.
>      
>      NBT is NetBios over TCP/IP.  This is required for an NT login, as 
>      differenciated from Telnet, FTP, or NFS;  each of which can be 
>      provided on NT and do not require NetBios. 
>      
>      In order to use TCP/IP as the only transport protocol for NT logins, 
>      WINS is required to resolve NetBios names for NT login (this is not 
>      exactly true but it's what you want to do).  And, if you are spanning 
>      more than one IP network with a router, you will want to use what MS 
>      calls H mode, look it up in the RK.  Most problems are taken care of 
>      when there is a WINS server on each net - but be careful on how 
>      replecation is setup between them or you'll never get logged in. 
