This problem is caused by the fact that deleting a user and 
recreating the user causes different SIDs to be assigned to
that account -- therefore the system sees them as completely
different users.  The system does warn you of this when you
attempt to delete a user.  The profile created for the first user
is not readable by the second user becuase a security
violation occurs.  The easiest way to recreate the user is
to restore the registry from when the user did exist.

