Aaron wrote:
>When I try to install 3.5 or 3.51, I get the following message during the 
>character cell "Windows NT Setup" during the "Setup is loading files..." 
>phase:
>
>     File \alpha\ntkrnlmp.exe could not be loaded.
>     The error code is 4
>
>     Setup cannot continue.  Press any key to exit.
>
>*Why* is this machine trying to load the mp kernel???  What can I do to get 
>around it?  What have I gotten crossed up?

The problem here Aaron is that you have probably run the OpenVMS/UNIX ECU and 
not the Windows NT ECU. The two ECUs setup the Adaptec SCSI Controller card 
differently depending on the operating system's requirements. You need to re-run 
the ECU when switching between OpenVMS/DigitalUNIX and Windows NT.

All Alpha systems currently load the file called ntkrnlmp during setup.

Gordon

