I've never heard anyone say that, but I can imagine why they would.  First,
there really is no difference between the "Alpha" and "Intel" versions of
NT, regardless of whom you buy it from.  However, Digital does do a couple
extras that are nice -- for example, I recently got the 3.51 stepup from
Digital and it included:

        Alpha ECU disk, v1.8 for NT (sly wink to Gordon)
        Alpha Firmware CD-ROM
        Windows NT RoadMap CD

So, if you've already got the latest ECU and Firmware, and if you don't
mind accessing the RoadMap over the Internet, don't worry about where you
get the kit.  On the other hand, if you don't have any of the above and
would like your own copy, get it from Digital.

>Yeuk K Cheung

Just my opinion,
Aaron

