From: Sakovich, Aaron <ASakovich@ncs.com>
Subject: RE: NT boot fails after firmware update

You can also do an Emergency Repair -- boot from the CD as if you were doing 
an install, then select Repair from the menu.  Stick in your Emergency 
Repair Disk (you *did* create an ERD, didn't you?) and tell it to check the 
boot files.

I have my users update their ERD's after successfully modifying their 
workstations in any fashion, be it password changes, new user additions, 
application installs, whatever.  They'll rotate through a pair of floppies 
so that there's a duplicate, also.  To update or create an ERD for your 
machine, start RDISK.

Aaron
