From: Sakovich, Aaron <ASakovich@ncs.com>
Subject: RE: Software Metering Applications

One possibility is to ensure that the application can be run via UNC's, then 
simply set a limit on the share for the number of connections that can be 
had. Using UNC's, the connection is broken as soon as the user exits the 
application, thereby not "wasting" a license.  This has the obvious benefits 
of being simple, free (when you buy NTS), easy to administer, and easy to 
run from the client's perspective.

All assuming that your application works with UNC's.  If not, then all bets 
are off...

Just a thought,
Aaron
