Just so there's no misunderstanding: If I understand you correctly,
you intend to test the Microsoft Windows NT Server from their CD-ROM
on the AlphaStation 250 4/266.  If that's the case, there's no reason
for you to get anything from Digital, since we get what we ship with
our platforms from Microsoft, in the first place; the Alpha version of
Windows NT Server 3.51 is on the same CD-ROM as the Intel version.  

There is no reason to expect you will have any problems installing 
Windows NT 3.51 Server from your CD-ROM on your workstation, but be 
aware that the AlphaStation 250 is not especially optimal for running 
Windows NT Server, relative, say, to an AlphaServer 1000 4/266, or the 
like.

