"concurrent licensing" usually applies to using the same license on two 
different PCs, but not at the same time.  For example, same license on both 
office and home PCs where you use only one at a time.  Unfortunately, 
this is very easily abused.

MS made matters worse by stating that SW license metering isn't 
sufficient for them.  You must buy as manny licenses as people able to 
access the file.  A network with 200 users requires 200 licenses even if 
only 20 use it.  MS's point is that it is too easy to change the numbers 
in the metering data base.  Sorta of like taking away car keys from all 
because a few drive drunk.

