Generally, I'd say it's a good practice to download and install SPs
as they become available. This will update your installation to the most
current build that's available. However, I would recommend waiting 1-2 
weeks after a SP is released, and monitor the major NT lists, to see if
anybody experiences problems with a particular SP. 

As for whether or not you actually *need* the SPs, there is a text file
available for download that identifies all the 'problems' that the SPs
eradicate. It's available at the same location as the SPs:

ftp://ftp.microsoft.com/bussys/winnt/winnt-public/fixes/NT351

Be sure to pick the appropriate platform -- in your case, Alpha.

Also, remember that SPs are cumulative; i.e., SP3 contains all the changes
in SP1 and SP2, so you don't need to get all of them.

Brian

