Subject: 	RE: NT boot fails after firmware update

Ron Diaz wrote:
>but now that I've re-re upgraded the firmware to run the ARC console for 
NT.
>I get the following message on attempted reboot:  
>Error: File is not a directory, press any key to continue.
>OSLOADER cannot be found, value is:
>    scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)\os\winnt\osloader.exe

When you upgrade the firmware it also destroys your environment variables 
(including the boot selections, default system partition etc). There are a 
pair 
of utilities on the firmware disks called saveenv.exe and restenv.exe which 
are 
used to save these settings then restore them after a firmware upgrade.

When the firmware is installed it sets up the environment variables to some 
default values, which may or may not work on your particular Windows NT 
installation. These are default values - check:

SYSTEMPARTITON  scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)
OSLOADER 	scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)\os\winnt\osloader.exe
                            ^ is this the ID of the disk NT is installed on?
                                                ^ big partition first?

OSLOADPARTITION scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
                            ^                   ^ same questions for OS 
partitition.

OSLOADFILENAME  \winnt35
                  ^ correct directory?

There is another utility on firmware floppies called ARCDOS.EXE which can be 

used to find the location of files on FAT partitions. 

To use ARCDOS use "Run a Program" from the ARC Console and supply the 
location 
of ARCDos (A:ARCDOS.EXE for a firmware floppy disk or 
CD:\CDROM\DEC2000\ARCDOS.EXE for firmware CDROM).

Type "cd scsi(0)disk(x)rdisk(0)partition(y)" to check what files are on 
partition. Just type "dir" to list files: If it says that it can't recognise 
the 
file system then it is either a foreign (or unformatted area) or NTFS 
formatted.

Gordon

