From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: HAL files

Craig,

You can, as you suggested, simply copy the desired HAL into the system 
partition - what you call the FAT area, replacing the hal.dll file that's 
hidden there (it is a hidden and system file, as is the O/S loader, 
osloader.exe).  Be sure to save the one that's there, as well, so that if 
you have a problem you can recover back to the original HAL.

That said, there is no special HAL needed for running Windows NT 3.51 on 
these platforms:

	AlphaServer 2000 4/200
	AlphaServer 2100 4/200
	AlphaServer 2100 5/250

The product name you mention is not one of those, and there are no others. 
 If your system is running Windows NT Server 3.51 now, please do not update 
your HAL, lest you kill your system.  If you have need for additional 
discussion, please feel free to e-mail me directly.

Cheers,
James

