All,

Brian's creative workaround clearly isn't for RISC systems, since you
don't get to dual-boot Windows 95 on one, but you'll be happy to hear
that the capability you really want is in the Shell Update Release, in
the form of a right mouse-button action on the task bar.  This brings
up a menu, one of the entries in which is "Task Control."  Selecting
this gets you a popup containing a list of the running applications for
selection, and the set of action buttons you're accustomed to from the
3.51 task manager, e.g., end, switch to, and the like.  Given that it's
all driven by mouse clicks (or key strokes, if that's your pleasure), I
think it's about as efficient a means of task management as 3.51 gives,
or marginally better, once you get used to it.

Cheers,
James

